KNOWNBUG
main.cpp

^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ through B: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ through C: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Assertion 2 fails, with pointer-outside-bounds failures: the virtual
pointer of the second A subobject (`A@vtable_pointer@/tag-C/tag-A', at C's
position in D) holds virtual_table::tag-A@tag-D@/tag-C/tag-A, a table of
type virtual_table::A.  The conversion from C to V reads it as a
virtual_table::C to get C's offset of V, which lies outside the smaller
table, so the V address and V::g's dispatch are wrong.  The repeated
subobject needs a table of the type of the class on its path (C).  Found
while testing construction vtables; the W188 build fails it the same way.
